1
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,540
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:31,500
Your moves!

3
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:06,400
Flight Commander KC-1, radar
indicates you've reached Egypt.

4
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:09,739
I could have told you that
by looking out my window.

5
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:17,300
You were right, Toshizu.

6
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:18,880
Kaiba did show up.

7
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:25,060
Who are you, the welcoming committee?

8
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:28,431
Don't tell me you've forgotten us already.

9
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:31,977
How could I forget the
three freaks that turned

10
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:35,060
my Battle City tournament
into a circus sideshow?

11
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:40,700
Now, if you'll step aside, I've
got some work to do. Don't bother.

12
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:44,637
I'm afraid what you've come here
to find is no longer in there.

13
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:45,600
Why's that?

14
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:49,160
The stone tablet has been
returned to its resting place.

15
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:51,720
That is what you seek, isn't it?

16
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:53,175
The Pharaoh's tablet?

17
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,510
Tablet?

18
00:01:54,593 --> 00:01:55,560
Not quite.

19
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:58,791
Then why did you come all this way, Kaiba?

20
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,620
Because of this.

21
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:08,136
That punk Bacora handed it to me just
before he walked out on our duel.

22
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:11,060
So I'm here to finish things. Bacora?

23
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:15,736
He must be planning to prevent the
pharaoh from fulfilling his destiny.

24
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,160
Oh, no.

25
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,940
We have to make sure he fails.

26
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:21,700
But how?

27
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,720
Kaiba, we need you.

28
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:25,892
So I'll make you a deal.

29
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:30,300
I'll help you locate Bakura if
you help us to save the Pharaoh.

30
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:35,900
I could do this every
single day. That's right.

31
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,944
Just bounce your troubles away.

32
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:41,280
Who's next? Our best.

33
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:44,435
I heard about Bakura.

34
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:47,537
So he's the evil force you
battled all those years ago.

35
00:02:47,620 --> 00:02:48,450
That's right.

36
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:50,760
And now he has our puzzle.

37
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:53,600
An item passed down to me by my father.

38
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,500
Your father?

39
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:58,040
Does that mean your memory's back?

40
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:01,760
Only a small piece.

41
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:04,040
A fragment of my childhood.

42
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:06,997
When I was prince.

43
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:09,260
When my father protected me.

44
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,917
He was a powerful leader who created the

45
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,937
Millennium Items in order
to restore peace to Egypt.

46
00:03:17,020 --> 00:03:20,377
But I'm afraid these seven
objects have a dark side as well.

47
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:24,837
Oh, so I guess that's why Bakura wants
to get a hold of him, right, Pharaoh?

48
00:03:24,920 --> 00:03:25,750
Correct.

49
00:03:25,833 --> 00:03:30,445
And I have to do everything in my power
to stop him, just like I did in the past.

50
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,621
Well, we're all here to help you.

51
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:35,671
Hey, did you ever learn what your name is?

52
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:38,600
See for yourself.

53
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,380
So it's still blank, huh?

54
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:44,620
No one here calls me by my real name.

55
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,557
They refer to me as King or Pharaoh.

56
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:50,080
Hey, Pharaoh, come on in.

57
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:52,140
The water's nice. High five.

58
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:59,400
Rest well, Kassara.

59
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:02,460
You possess a gift that might save us.

60
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:24,240
Now that your secret is out, Master Aknadin
wants to take that power away from you.

61
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:27,637
What puzzles me is how a
man who built his reputation

62
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:30,860
on giving mercy to criminals
can be so heartless.

63
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:33,965
When I first entered the
Pharaoh's royal court,

64
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:37,060
it was Aknadin who taught
me compassion and reason.

65
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:41,000
But now I hardly recognize him.

66
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:43,457
Master Settle!

67
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:46,037
I just received word that
the Pharaoh's all right!

68
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,980
I knew it. Where is he?

69
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:50,652
On the south bank of the River Nile, sir.

70
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:55,380
Quickly, move that girl to a different
room and make sure no one sees you.

71
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:02,340
Members of the Royal Guard,
I bring you joyous news.

72
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:04,540
The Pharaoh has been found.

73
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,671
According to my necklace,

74
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:12,251
our king is in good health and Shadda
will see to it that he returns safely.

75
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:15,960
We can all rest easy now

76
00:05:16,620 --> 00:05:18,540
Yes, his highness is safe

77
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:21,860
Impossible, how could he have survived?

78
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:23,730
Wait,

79
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:29,137
I'm seeing something else Oh
no I have some terrible news

80
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:33,180
regarding the pharaoh's
millennium puzzle It's missing

81
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:38,120
Who are you?

82
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:40,910
That's...

83
00:05:40,993 --> 00:05:43,586
You are a lot shorter
than I thought you'd be.

84
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:45,260
Ha ha ha ha!

85
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:47,080
I kid you!

86
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:52,440
Uh, Pharaoh meet our newest friend and
honorary member of the gang, Mofasa.

87
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:57,677
If it hadn't been for all his help, there's
no way we would have ever found you.

88
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:58,590
Oh, Shuts!

89
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:00,220
You are making me blush!

90
00:06:00,460 --> 00:06:02,420
Mofasa, pleasure to meet you.

91
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:06,560
My king, the pleasure is all mine.

92
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:12,450
Pharaoh!

93
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:20,360
My Pharaoh, it's true. You're safe.

94
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:23,073
Yes, I'm sorry to have alarmed everyone.

95
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:26,020
So he can't see me, right? You! Hey!

96
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:27,620
Mana, halt!

97
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:29,800
Hi, Shaddaa!

98
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:31,509
Didn't even see you there!

99
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:35,160
You knew his whereabouts all along? Maybe.

100
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:37,440
Ballsy means business.

101
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:43,020
More importantly, we found
Bakura's hiding spot Excellent

102
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:49,340
We have traced his trail to a deserted
village It was once known as Kol Elna

103
00:06:51,300 --> 00:06:52,320
Alright men,

104
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:55,440
to Kol Elna Hold it right there,

105
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:59,477
we're coming too It's much too
dangerous for you to join me

106
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:03,442
Bakura has challenged me to a
shadow game with the ultimate stakes

107
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:09,200
You should all go back to your
world and let me deal with mine.

108
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:12,180
Pharaoh, come back!

109
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:13,900
Nice meeting you!

110
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:17,037
I'm telling you, he needs
all the help he can get.

111
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:17,960
From us?

112
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:21,500
Joey, we can't even pick
up an apple in this world.

113
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:23,020
So how can we help?

114
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:26,205
I don't know, but I'm
not quitting that easily.

115
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:28,410
Joey's right.

116
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:31,177
The Pharaoh would never
give up on us, right?

117
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:32,180
No way.

118
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:35,177
And we're not going to
give up on him either.

119
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:36,090
You're right.

120
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:38,110
Absolutely!

121
00:07:38,193 --> 00:07:39,023
But first we eat.

122
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:44,380
So Bakura's in the village
of Kal-El-Nah? Yes.

123
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:47,420
The Pharaoh and Shadda
are on their way now.

124
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:52,160
We must join them and
protect our king. Right.

125
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:54,777
Oh no.

126
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:56,280
Not Kal-El-Nah.

127
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:01,292
I believe it's just ahead, your highness.

128
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:10,180
What is this place?

129
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:15,360
I am told this village was once
populated with criminals and deviants.

130
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:18,820
And one day they just disappeared.

131
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:26,340
I've heard this town
is inhabited by ghosts.

132
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:30,200
I have an idea.

133
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:32,697
Let's leave a note for
Bakura and ask him if he

134
00:08:32,780 --> 00:08:34,717
wouldn't mind meeting us
somewhere that isn't haunted.

135
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:36,160
Anyone with me?

136
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:40,020
I guess I'll take that as a null.

137
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:57,700
Help! Help!

138
00:08:58,100 --> 00:08:59,220
We're surrounded!

139
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:09,000
All right, my friends, the time has come.

140
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:12,160
It appears his royal majesty has arrived.

141
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:18,260
Welcome to my humble aboot, Pharaoh,
where I have the home field advantage.

142
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:26,660
Take this!

143
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:29,040
What are these things?

144
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:32,180
Hold your ground!

145
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,920
We must protect our king!

146
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:37,640
Mana, you have the power to defeat them.

147
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:38,920
Be strong.

148
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:42,100
You don't need to protect me.

149
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:45,780
I should really be the one protecting you.

150
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:50,000
If I want to be one of your
elite spellcasters someday,

151
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:52,655
then I need to stop hiding behind you.

152
00:09:52,980 --> 00:09:56,880
If Mahad were here, he'd say
the same thing. Very well.

153
00:09:58,660 --> 00:10:00,840
Two-headed jackal warrior! Attack!

154
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:09,760
We'll fight.

155
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:12,580
You fight, Bakura. Good luck. Right.

156
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:14,782
And the same to you, my friends.

157
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:26,060
Not to worry, my friends.

158
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:28,300
Soon revenge will be ours.

159
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:32,280
The son shall pay for
the sins of his father.

160
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:41,240
Show yourself, Bakura.

161
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,840
I know you're in here.

162
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:51,400
I must say I'm impressed, Farrow.

163
00:10:51,980 --> 00:10:54,477
Your father never had
the courage to come here,

164
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:57,140
which makes him a wiser man than you.

165
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,400
Mana, watch out!

166
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:14,820
Uh, nicely done.

167
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:24,207
I see your back from
the edge of the shadows.

168
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,518
Well, not for long.

169
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:27,530
Let's duel.

170
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:31,061
There's something you
should have a look at first.

171
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:36,860
Is that the legendary
Millennium Stone Tablet?

172
00:11:37,220 --> 00:11:38,860
The one and only.

173
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:43,140
And as you can see, each of the
seven items fit neatly inside.

174
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:45,014
Oh, and did I mention?

175
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:50,022
The stone is guarded by the very spirits
who were imprisoned in order to create it.

176
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:53,877
Your father destroyed their
village and captured their

177
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:57,520
souls in an attempt to gain
the power to dominate mankind.

178
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:59,920
How do I know, you ask?

179
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:02,777
Because I am the only
villager who escaped.

180
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:05,680
The sole survivor, if you will.

181
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:11,108
My father created the Millennium Items
to bring peace and prosperity to Egypt.

182
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:12,210
Understand?

183
00:12:12,380 --> 00:12:16,137
I understand that's what you've been
told by your so-called guardians.

184
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:17,120
But they lied.

185
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:19,994
Now spirits open his eyes to the truth.

186
00:12:23,340 --> 00:12:26,260
Soon your spirit shall
join theirs, Pharaoh.

187
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:28,620
Trapped for all eternity.

188
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:34,800
And without your millennium
puzzle, you're powerless.

189
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:36,990
Finally,

190
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:41,845
after years of hiding in the darkest
shadows, the town of Kal 'Elna strikes back.

191
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:43,280
It's almost poetic.

192
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:00,400
What's this?

193
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:07,100
When you threaten the
Pharaoh, you threaten me. You!

194
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:09,000
My heart!

195
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:10,380
Oh, I see.

196
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:15,357
Getting destroyed once wasn't enough, so
you decided to come back for round two.

197
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,200
I'm here to save my king.

198
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:20,397
You don't have to put
yourself in harm's way again.

199
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:23,120
I made a vow to always
protect you, Pharaoh.

200
00:13:24,020 --> 00:13:27,902
That promise will hold true no
matter how powerful our foe may be.

201
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:30,360
Mahad, tell me,

202
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:35,620
did my father truly destroy a village
in order to forge the Millennium Items?

203
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:41,220
Excuse me, I can answer that, seeing
as I was there when it all happened.

204
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:45,980
And believe me, it was an
evening that I'll never forget.

205
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:50,857
I watched in horror as your
father's henchmen harnessed the

206
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:55,240
spirits of my fellow villagers
to further his own selfish needs.

207
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,657
How could he? My...

208
00:13:57,740 --> 00:13:59,520
my own father?

209
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:04,766
What Bakura has failed to mention is that
every citizen of his village was evil.

210
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:07,140
But how do you know that?

211
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:10,535
I always sensed the darkness
within my Millennium Ring.

212
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:14,240
So I began to research the
spell used to create it.

213
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:17,109
I then reported my
findings to your father.

214
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:21,968
And he was as surprised as I was when
he learned what had occurred at Kolelna.

215
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:23,800
Oh no.

216
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:25,170
No.

217
00:14:25,253 --> 00:14:28,140
How can these items bring peace
if they're plagued by evil?

218
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:29,657
It's not your fault, sir.

219
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:30,681
You didn't know.

220
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:35,980
Bahad, I am the king of Egypt.

221
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:40,240
Every task carried out by my
guards is my responsibility.

222
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:47,900
And now, I must pay by confessing
my crime to the Egyptian gods.

223
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,780
He was innocent!

224
00:14:51,580 --> 00:14:54,137
Your father took the blame
so that you could continue

225
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:58,360
his legacy by finally bringing
peace to the land of Egypt.

226
00:14:58,960 --> 00:14:59,800
You're right.

227
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:02,300
Are you two finished yet?

228
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:07,080
Now, my spirits, destroy
both of these fools!

229
00:15:08,580 --> 00:15:13,397
By bringing the Millennium Items into this
world, I have unleashed a great threat.

230
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:14,940
My reign will soon end.

231
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:19,337
But please guide my son so that he
may use these items to restore peace.

232
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:21,960
My father was a worthy king,

233
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:25,477
and I owe it to him to take you down and

234
00:15:25,560 --> 00:15:28,384
return this land to the
prosperity it once knew!

235
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:34,457
In the name of the former Pharaoh,

236
00:15:34,540 --> 00:15:37,481
return your Millennium
items to where they belong!

237
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:41,080
And I suppose you think
they belong with you.

238
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:43,599
If you were truly paying attention,

239
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:47,117
you'd know that the items are meant to
be back in their original resting place.

240
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:49,940
And that's exactly where
I plan to put them.

241
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:52,940
Never have it your way.

242
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:57,400
Now, Deerbound, come forth.

243
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:07,180
As you can see,

244
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:12,157
thanks to the power of my Millennium
Items, my Deerbound has evolved once again.

245
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:16,020
And once I destroy you, his
strength will know no bounds.

246
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:18,840
Bahaad, be careful!

247
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:22,300
Diabound, Thunderboss, attack!

248
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:28,700
Dark Magic Portal!

249
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,100
What's that?

250
00:16:31,420 --> 00:16:36,360
Behold, this Vortex will absorb
your attack and redirect its target.

251
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:39,080
So your assault has backfired!

252
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:46,550
No!

253
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,741
It'll crush the Millennium Stone!

254
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:50,940
Deerbound, stop that pillar!

255
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,600
Nice try, Mahal!

256
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:03,180
Attack all you want!

257
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:05,301
You'll never defeat my Deerbound!

258
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:08,217
And if you think he's a
force to be reckoned with,

259
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:11,182
Then just wait until you
meet Zork, the Dark One.

260
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:13,560
Did you say Zork?

261
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:16,780
Zork, the Dark One, will awaken you.

262
00:17:17,780 --> 00:17:21,400
This stone tablet conceals
the source of my true power.

263
00:17:22,020 --> 00:17:25,820
So I shall call upon another
shadow creature to protect it.

264
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:29,180
Meet my skeleton fiend.

265
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:30,620
Two beasts?

266
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:34,000
Yes, double the
destruction, double the fun.

267
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:36,917
Now, is anyone up for a
game of hide and seek?

268
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,460
Well, I am.

269
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:42,840
Look! His creature!

270
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,140
It's gone!

271
00:17:44,580 --> 00:17:46,520
We mustn't let it get away!

272
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:48,920
Rapid spell fire!

273
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:02,440
My Deabaum is concealed by the darkness,
so trying to attack him is pointless.

274
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,880
We weren't attacking him

275
00:18:09,620 --> 00:18:12,700
No, but how did you expose my creature?

276
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:18,960
We simply brightened up the room to penetrate
the darkness Now, Maha, finish him off

277
00:18:25,620 --> 00:18:28,160
It's over Not yet

278
00:18:30,660 --> 00:18:33,400
Your spellcaster may
have improved his skills,

279
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:37,400
but I'm afraid he's still not
good enough to keep me down!

280
00:18:39,940 --> 00:18:44,380
Now, Doxipirix, fill me with your
power so I may avenge your suffering!

281
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:55,457
It's even stronger now!

282
00:18:55,540 --> 00:18:56,937
Quickly, Mahat!

283
00:18:57,020 --> 00:19:02,080
He blocked it!

284
00:19:02,660 --> 00:19:03,620
See about!

285
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:05,180
Spiral wave attack!

286
00:19:08,720 --> 00:19:10,220
No! Mahat!

287
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:13,540
Time to seal your friend
away for all eternity!

288
00:19:14,340 --> 00:19:15,340
Lightning blast!

289
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,417
Ah, game over.

290
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:26,640
Your dark magician is no more.

291
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:28,460
This can't be.

292
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:30,340
Mahad is safe, my pharaoh.

293
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:33,537
But how?

294
00:19:33,620 --> 00:19:35,240
Who summoned you?

295
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:37,380
A former student of yours.

296
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:41,330
Mana!

297
00:19:41,900 --> 00:19:43,841
Thought you might need some help.
